    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5630d34e_3155ccb9",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/rand.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T12:09:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should there be some sort of sleep in this loop between retries? I guess a wait for interrupt isn\u0027t necessarily the right thing.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "cb0340c3600a6c6ab6c2cbc40502f61b78c34c4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a880d70_12d9699d",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/rand.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T12:18:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t really have support for `WFI`-like sleep but we could easily busy sleep; but how would we pick the duration? What are you concerned about? The extra load on the system/host? Hopefully, it shouldn\u0027t be noticeable given how getting entropy is a one-time thing.\n\nTo reduce the number of calls, we could also look into integrating a TRNG-seeded PRNG ...",
      "parentUuid": "5630d34e_3155ccb9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "cb0340c3600a6c6ab6c2cbc40502f61b78c34c4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e113a0eb_f3e5384c",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/rand.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T12:20:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No particular reason, busy waits just always make me feel bad.\nHopefully the entropy becomes available in a reasonable time.",
      "parentUuid": "7a880d70_12d9699d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "cb0340c3600a6c6ab6c2cbc40502f61b78c34c4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "beb7ada1_5319a0cd",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/rand.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T12:25:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We don\u0027t really have support for WFI-like sleep\n\nWhy not? Just `asm!(\"wfi\")`, no?",
      "parentUuid": "e113a0eb_f3e5384c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "cb0340c3600a6c6ab6c2cbc40502f61b78c34c4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "05690f66_cc29521e",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/rand.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T14:05:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it that simple? Doesn\u0027t the interrupt come from a timer, for which we\u0027d need a driver? Does this also require an interrupt handler to filter out spurious wake-ups?\n\nAnyway, how could we figure out how long to sleep, as that will depend on the EL3 implementation?",
      "parentUuid": "beb7ada1_5319a0cd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "cb0340c3600a6c6ab6c2cbc40502f61b78c34c4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7adcabd5_5908202d",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/rand.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T14:13:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, there\u0027s no obvious reason to believe that there will be an interrupt when the entropy is ready, or indeed ever.",
      "parentUuid": "05690f66_cc29521e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "cb0340c3600a6c6ab6c2cbc40502f61b78c34c4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "36149fec_ed417979",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/rand.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T14:27:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would WFE get triggered? That\u0027s the one used in spinlocks, but i think it might depend on another thread doing atomic writes.",
      "parentUuid": "7adcabd5_5908202d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "cb0340c3600a6c6ab6c2cbc40502f61b78c34c4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5b04b4e_40c6e115",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/rand.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T16:09:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can only get the entropy from non-blocking `SMCCC_TRNG_RND` calls so the `WFI` would NOT be triggered by EL3 and/or the entropy source, but by _something_ (probably a timer) attempting to guess when EL3 has replenished its entropy pool.\n\nI\u0027m not sure what `WFE` on a uniprocessor at EL1 would do/mean in the context of a single-threaded baremetal application as no other vCPU would generate the event we would be waiting for?",
      "parentUuid": "36149fec_ed417979",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "cb0340c3600a6c6ab6c2cbc40502f61b78c34c4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dc340193_57b0f228",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/rand.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T16:10:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, nvm. Let\u0027s leave it as is. The pVM is still preemptible...",
      "parentUuid": "a5b04b4e_40c6e115",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
